<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Italy (medieval)</h1><p class="st-meta">888 CE – 1801 CE (approx.) · capital Pavia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The medieval Kingdom of Italy, contested by Italian magnates after 888 and then held by the German emperors, whose authority waned as the cities grew.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> broke up in 888, Italian nobles elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy">Berengar of Friuli</a> as King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. For seventy years rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a> and outsiders, among them Guy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lambert-of-italy">Lambert of Spoleto</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-blind">Louis of Provence</a>, Rudolf of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-of-arles">Hugh of Arles</a>, fought for the crown, which was traditionally received at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-pavia">Pavia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 951 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> took the title, and from his imperial coronation in 962 the crown was tied to the German emperors, often crowned with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-crown-of-lombardy">Iron Crown of Lombardy</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arduin-of-ivrea">Arduin of Ivrea</a> was the last native king (1002–1014). Imperial rule relied on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and counts, but the communes grew independent; the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnano">Legnano</a> in 1176, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-constance">Peace of Constance</a> in 1183 recognised their self-government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the 13th century the kingdom survived mainly as a legal framework of imperial fiefs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> was the last emperor crowned King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-bologna">Bologna</a> in 1530. Imperial claims in Italy ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-luneville">Treaty of Lunéville</a> in 1801.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-italy-medieval.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Italy (medieval)" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo, eagle by N3MO · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Holy_Roman_Emperor_with_haloes_(1430-1806).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>888 CE – 1801 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pavia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Berengar I, Otto I, Arduin of Ivrea</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Regnum Italiae, Regnum Italicum, Imperial Italy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1344&amp;focus=kingdom-of-italy-medieval" aria-label="Kingdom of Italy (medieval) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4898 583 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Italy (medieval) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5218 839L5218 839M5218 839L5308 915M5218 839L5218 839M5218 839L5229 694M5218 839L5308 809M5218 839L51